          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \omega)
            regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+system"} physical system
            %em polarization
            is, locally, a choice of decomposition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            into “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinates"}> canonical coordinates
            ” and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momenta"}> canonical momenta
            ”.
          %p
            The archetypical example is that where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = T^* \Sigma
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinates"} canonical coordinates
            are those parameterizing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            itself, while the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momenta"} canonical momenta
            are coordinates on each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            of the cotangent bundle.
          %p
            But for general symplectic manifolds there is no such canonical choice of coordinates and momenta. Moreover, in general there is not even a global notion of canonical momenta. Instead, a choice of (real) polarization is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
            of phase space by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifolds"} Lagrangian submanifolds
            and then
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinates"}> canonical coordinates
                ” are coordinates on the corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaf+space"} leaf space
                (parameterizing the leaves);
            %li
              %p
                the “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momenta"}> canonical momenta
                ” are coordinates along each
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaf"} leaf
                %em typical leaf
                then this is not a globally defined notion, only the polarization itself is.
          %p
            Locally this is a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+patch"} coordinate patch
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \mathbb{R}^{2n} \to X
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
            takes the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mi ω
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∧
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi^* \omega = \sum_{i = 1}^n \mathbf{d} q^i \wedge \mathbf{d}p_i
          %p
            where the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{q^i : \mathbb{R}^{2n} \simeq \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}\}
            are the canonical coordinates on the first
            = succeed "-factor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi o
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p_o : \mathbb{R}^{2n} \simeq \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}\}
            are canonical coordinates on the second
            = succeed "-factor." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The traditional notion of polarization applies to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#OfASymplecticManifold"} Of a symplectic manifold
          %p
            Symplectic manifold are the lowest step in a tower of notions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+symplectic+geometry"} higher symplectic geometry
            which proceeds with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+geometry"} n-plectic geometry
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and manifolds refined to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoids"} smooth infinity-groupoids
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroids"} symplectic Lie n-algebroids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroids"} Poisson Lie algebroids
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            are
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+Lie+2-algebroids"} Courant Lie 2-algebroids
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#OfAPoissonLieAlgebroid"} Of a Poisson Lie algebroid
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#OfACourantLie2Algebroid"} Of a Courant Lie 2-algebroid
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#OfASymplecticLienAlgebroid"} Of a symplectic Lie n-algebroid
          %h3#OfASymplecticManifold Of a symplectic manifold
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \omega)
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
          #ByLagrangianFoliation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong real polarization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \omega)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifolds"} Lagrangian submanifolds
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Weinstein"}> Weinstein, p. 9
            ).
          %p More generally
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong polarization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
              is a choice of involutive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+subspace"} Lagrangian subbundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P} \hookrightarrow T_{\mathbb{C}} X
              of of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexification"} complexified
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#BatesWeinstein"}> Bates-Weinstein, def. 7.4
            )
          %h3#OfAPoissonLieAlgebroid Of a Poisson Lie algebroid
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔓
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{P}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            as the algebra of functions on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifold"} dg-manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          #ForPoissonLieAlgebroidyByLagrangianFoliation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A dg-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifold"} Lagrangian submanifold
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔓
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
              is also called a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Λ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
                  \-structure
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Severa"} Ševera, section 4
            %p
              Hence we might say
              %strong real polarization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔓
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
              is a foliation by dg-Lagrangian submanifolds.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \pi)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
              underlying a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔓
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔓
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
              corresponds to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coisotropic+submanifold"} coisotropic submanifold
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \pi)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Severa"}> Ševera, section 4
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The dg-Lagrangian submanifolds also correspond to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
              (see there) on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔓
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{P}, \omega)
          %h3#OfACourantLie2Algebroid Of a Courant Lie 2-algebroid
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+Lie+algebroid"} Courant Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℭ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{C}
            is a
