          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %h3#quantum_states_and_wave_functions Quantum states and wave functions
          %p
            Upon (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"}> geometric
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the physical system described by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \omega)
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            is supposed to be a function on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            – or rather a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            which is a “wave-function that only depends on the canonical coordinates”, not on the canonical momenta. In terms of polarizations this is formalized by saying that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states+%28in+geometric+quantization%29"} quantum state
            is a section which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+derivative"} covariant constant
            along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaves"} leaves
            of the polarization (along the “momentum direction”).
          %h3#bohrsommerfeld_leaves Bohr-Sommerfeld leaves
          %p
            After a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            lifting
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bohr-Sommerfeld+leaf"} Bohr-Sommerfeld leaf
            of a (real) polarization is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leaf"} leaf
            on which the prequantum line bundle is not just flat, but also trivializable as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+bundle"} circle bundle
            with connection.
          %h3#liouville_integrability Liouville integrability
          %p
            If a polarization on an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
