                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarized+algebraic+variety"} polarized algebraic variety
          %h2#references References
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul#Weinstein
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
              ,
              %em Lectures on Symplectic manifolds
              Lecture 2
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lagrangian splittings, real and complex polarizations, Kähler manifolds
          %ul#BatesWeinstein
            %li
              Sean Bates,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"} Alan Weinstein
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures on the geometry of quantization
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.berkeley.edu/~alanw/GofQ.pdf"} pdf
          %ul
            %li
              Kristin Shaw,
              %em An introduction to polarizations
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.toronto.edu/karshon/grad/2006-07/polarizations.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p and section 4 and 5 of
          %ul#Blau
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Blau"}> Matthias Blau
              ,
              %em Symplectic Geometry and Geometric Quantization
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BlauGeometricQuantization.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p or section 5 of
          %ul
            %li
              A. Echeverria-Enriquez, M.C. Munoz-Lecanda, N. Roman-Roy, C. Victoria-Monge,
              %em Mathematical Foundations of Geometric Quantization
              Extracta Math. 13 (1998) 135-238 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/9904008"}> arXiv:math-ph/9904008
              )
          %p or
          %ul
            %li
              Yuichi Nohara,
              %em Independence of Polarization in Geometric Quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://geoquant2007.mi.ras.ru/nohara.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Lagrangian submanifolds of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebroids"} L-infinity algebroids
            are considered in
          %ul
            %li#Severa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavol+%C5%A0evera"}> Pavol Ševera
              ,
              %em Some title containing the words “homotopy” and “symplectic”, e.g. this one
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105080"}> arXiv:0105080
              )
          %p
            In the case that the polarization integrates to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            one may think of passing to polarized sections as equivalent to passing to
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+equivalence"} gauge equivalence classes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel+Catren"}> Gabriel Catren
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the Relation Between Gauge and Phase Symmetries
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://philpapers.org/rec/CATOTR"} web
          %p
            More on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+polarizations"} real polarizations
          %ul
            %li
              Pau Mir,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eva+Miranda"} Eva Miranda
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric quantization via cotangent models
              %strong 11
              (2021) 118 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s13324-021-00559-4"}> doi:10.1007/s13324-021-00559-4
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.02699"} arXiv:2102.02699
          %p
            A candidate for polarizations for higher geometric quantization in
            = succeed "-plectic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li#Rogers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
              ,
              %em Higher symplectic geometry
              PhD thesis (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4068"}> arXiv:1106.4068
              ).
